      "name": null,
      "problem": "A radioactive substance decays exponentially such that its mass reduces by $\\frac{1}{4}$ every hour. If the mass of the substance was initially $2\\,\\text{kg},$ what is the mass of the substance after $9$ hours?",
      "worked_solution": "If the mass reduces by $\\frac{1}{4},$ then $\\frac{3}{4}$ of its mass remains every hour.\n\nTherefore:\n\n- After $1$ hour, the mass is $2\\cdot (\\frac{3}{4}).$\n\n- After $2$ hours, the mass is $2\\cdot {(\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}.$\n\n- After $3$ hours, the mass is $2\\cdot {(\\frac{3}{4})}^{3}.$\n\n- $…$\n\nRepeating this pattern, we see that the mass after $9$ hours is $2\\cdot {(\\frac{3}{4})}^{9}\\,\\text{kg}.$",
